1. NVIDIA Isaac Lab, branch exp/microduck, commit 802b8d5
   https://github.com/isaac-sim/IsaacLab
   Copyright (c) 2022-2026, The Isaac Lab Project Developers. BSD-3-Clause
   (full text: licenses/LICENSE-isaaclab-BSD-3-Clause).
   Adapted from source/isaaclab_tasks/isaaclab_tasks/contrib/microduck_obstacle:
   - sensors.py: the ToF impairment model (src/microduck_nav/impairments.py)
   - mdp/actions.py: the residual command processing (src/microduck_nav/residual_action.py)
   - agents/navigation_distribution.py: the guarded Beta mean (src/microduck_nav/nav_export.py)
   - mdp/events.py: the nine obstacle layout families and their bounds (src/microduck_nav/layouts.py)
   - mdp/geometry.py, mdp/commands.py, mdp/rewards.py: clearance, progress and risk maths, the goal arrival
     and obstacle bypass terms (src/microduck_nav/nav_math.py, rewards.py), the destination request
     (src/microduck_nav/commands.py)
   - mdp/terminations.py, mdp/observations.py, obstacle_avoidance_env_cfg.py, agents/rsl_rl_ppo_cfg.py: the
     collision and boundary terms, the observation terms, the task layout and weights, the PPO settings
     (src/microduck_nav/terminations.py, observations.py, env_cfg.py, rl_cfg.py)
   and from scripts/deploy/microduck_tof_nav/nav_pad.py: command_from_action, the ONNX contract.
   The tests run NVIDIA's own rewards.py, geometry.py and commands.py unmodified from a local clone
   (tests/nvidia_stubs.py); the clone is not part of this repository.

2. Pollen Robotics microduck_rl (mjlab_microduck), commit 0daab160
   Apache-2.0. Used as a git dependency pinned to the commit; not copied into this repository, except that
   src/microduck_nav/tof_geometry.py reproduces the zone-direction construction of
   src/mjlab_microduck/sim/tof.py (lines 50-62). The robot meshes of microduck_rl are
   CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0 (LICENSE-MODELS.md there) and are not part of this repository.
   The walking policy used in tests is read from the operator's local cache and is not committed.
